section section 7 3 b is:

section section 7 3 b 1 is:

tentative else recommended decision will contain a final EIS for a decision if
    it is not the case that
        the action of the decision is an action that may have a significant adverse effect on the environment
        and the action that may have a significant adverse effect on the environment has been withdrawn
    and it is not the case that the decision has on the basis of the record of the proceeding including the draft EIS as well as any comments received thereon the administrative law judge issuing this decision determined that the action will not have a significant adverse effect on the environment.

section section 7 3 b 2 is:

the determining issuance for final EIS for a decision with a cause for extension is a final EIS issuance if
    it is not the case that tentative else recommended decision will contain a final EIS for the decision
    and the final EIS issuance is equal to no_issuance
    otherwise it is not the case that nothing is equal to the cause for extension
    and the final EIS issuance is equal to issued_extended_beyond_45_days_of_the_close_of_the_record
    otherwise the final EIS issuance is equal to issued_within_45_days_of_the_close_of_the_record.

the closing date for a decision is a number N if
    the closing date of the proceeding record of the decision is a date D
    and N = D + 45.

the determining days till issuance for final EIS for a decision with a cause for extension with a days of extension D is a number if
    tentative else recommended decision will contain a final EIS for the decision
    and the never is the number
    otherwise it is not the case that nothing is equal to the cause for extension
    and the closing date for the decision is a number N
    and a date M = N + (45 + D)
    and the day number of M is the number
    otherwise the closing date for the decision is a third number
    and the day number of the third number is the number.

section section 7 3 b 3 is:

notice of no significant adverse effect on the environment determination will be filed in accordance with 6 NYCRR 617 10 for a decision if
    the decision has on the basis of the record of the proceeding including the draft EIS as well as any comments received thereon the administrative law judge issuing this decision determined that the action will not have a significant adverse effect on the environment.

copies of a decision together with a notice of its completion will be filed in accordance with 6 NYCRR 617 10 if
    tentative else recommended decision will contain a final EIS for the decision.

section section 7 3 c is:

